orow(19, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU HAVE COME TO THE HILL COUNTRY OF THE AMORITES WHICH THE LORD OUR GOD GIVES US" (1:20) — A PARABLE: A KING GAVE HIS SON TO A TUTOR, WHO WALKED HIM ROUND AND SHOWED HIM: ALL THESE VINES ARE YOURS, ALL THESE OLIVES ARE YOURS; WHEN HE TIRED OF SHOWING HIM HE SAID: ALL THAT YOU SEE IS YOURS. SO ALL THE FORTY YEARS THAT ISRAEL WAS IN THE WILDERNESS MOSES SAID TO THEM "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU INTO A GOOD LAND, A LAND OF BROOKS OF WATER, SPRINGS AND DEEPS FLOWING IN VALLEY AND HILL" (8:7); WHEN THEY CAME TO THE LAND HE SAID: YOU HAVE COME. IF YOU SAY THE TIME HAS NOT COME — IT HAS COME. The row on 1:20 ({SP_(19, 2, "כך", "כל", "ארבעים", "שנה", "שהיו", "ישראל", "במדבר")} "so all the forty years that Israel was in the wilderness"): 8:7 READ AS THE WILDERNESS\'S FORTY-YEAR REFRAIN — the tutor\'s "these vines, these olives" beside the chapter\'s own catalogue of the Land (8:7-9), and the parable\'s two stages the chapter\'s two clocks (the way of forty years 8:2, the good land 8:7); the ink: "a good land" twelve seats, 8:7 and 8:10 two of them; "these forty years" 2:7, 8:2, 8:4 (computed). Read before at sitting 1 (the 1:1-3:29 ledger, MATERIAL on 1:20); REREAD WHOLE here — the whole-row rule. Both files cite 8:7 in the same place (asserted).')
orow(32, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'R. MEIR SAYS: SEE, IT SAYS "AND YOU SHALL KNOW WITH YOUR HEART THAT AS A MAN DISCIPLINES HIS SON THE LORD YOUR GOD DISCIPLINES YOU" (8:5) — YOU AND YOUR HEART KNOW THE DEEDS YOU DID AND THE CHASTISEMENTS I BROUGHT ON YOU: NOT ACCORDING TO YOUR DEEDS DID I BRING THEM. The row on 6:5 ({SP_(32, 10, "אתה", "ולבך", "יודעים", "מעשים", "שעשית")} "you and your heart know the deeds you did"): 8:5\'s "with your heart" read as the sinner\'s own knowledge that the chastisement is lighter than the deed — the discipline of a son the measure. Read before at chapter 6 (CONTEXT on 6:5); reread whole here. The compile\'s row (Berakhot 5a\'s afflictions of love the kin).')
orow(32, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'R. NATHAN SON OF R. JOSEPH SAYS: AS A COVENANT IS CUT FOR THE LAND, SO A COVENANT IS CUT FOR CHASTISEMENTS, AS IT SAYS "THE LORD YOUR GOD DISCIPLINES YOU" (8:5) AND IT SAYS "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU INTO A GOOD LAND" (8:7). The row on 6:5 ({SP_(32, 12, "כשם", "שברית", "כרותה", "לארץ", "כך", "ברית", "כרותה")} "as a covenant is cut for the land, so a covenant is cut"): THE JUXTAPOSITION READ — 8:5 (the discipline) and 8:7 (the good land) stand two verses apart with 8:6 between them, and the shelf reads the neighbours as one covenant with two terms; the ink: 8:5 and 8:7 are the chapter\'s two "for" clauses (כי at 8:3, 3, 5, 7, 18, 19 — computed), the Land and the chastisement both given "for" — the shelf\'s move the neighbouring clauses read together (the shelf\'s own "and it says"). The English adds a citation the Hebrew quotes without one ("(Dt.8:5)" — the verse quoted in both files; asserted). Read before at chapter 6; reread whole here.')
orow(32, 15, 'CONTEXT', f'THE LAND OF ISRAEL — WHENCE? "THE LORD YOUR GOD DISCIPLINES YOU … FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU INTO A GOOD LAND" (8:5-7). The row on 6:5 ({SP_(32, 15, "ארץ", "ישראל", "מנין")} "the land of Israel — whence?"): the three goods given through suffering (the Torah, the Land, the world to come — the piska\'s list) — the Land\'s proof the same pair, 8:5 with 8:7. THE RANGE CITATION "(דברים ח ה-ז)" ("Deuteronomy 8:5-7") — the Hebrew\'s form the citation regex does not read; found through the English\'s "(Dt.8:5-7)" and asserted by string. Read before at chapter 6; reread whole here.')
orow(37, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON SON OF YOHAI SAYS: "THE WORLD" (PROVERBS 8:26) — THIS IS THE LAND OF ISRAEL, AS IT SAYS "REJOICING IN THE WORLD OF HIS EARTH" (8:31). WHY IS IT CALLED THE WORLD? BECAUSE IT IS SPICED WITH EVERYTHING: OTHER LANDS HAVE WHAT THIS ONE LACKS AND LACK WHAT THIS ONE HAS, BUT THE LAND OF ISRAEL LACKS NOTHING, AS IT SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT LACK ANYTHING IN IT" (8:9). The row on 11:10 ({SP_(37, 5, "אבל", "ארץ", "ישראל", "אינה", "חסרה", "כלום")} "but the land of Israel lacks nothing"): 8:9\'s "you shall not lack anything in it" read as the Land\'s completeness — a name explained by a sound (the world / spiced), the verse the proof; the ink: "you shall not lack anything" ONE seat, 2:7\'s "you lacked nothing" its wilderness twin, the verb\'s seven Torah seats (computed). The middah: the name read for its sound (the shelf\'s own). Fresh in both files.')
orow(39, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON SON OF YOHAI SAYS: TWELVE LANDS WERE GIVEN, AGAINST THE TWELVE TRIBES OF ISRAEL, AND THE TASTE OF ONE TRIBE\'S FRUIT IS NOT THE TASTE OF ANOTHER\'S — AND THESE ARE THEY: "THE LAND WHICH YOU GO IN TO POSSESS" (11:10), "THE LAND WHICH YOU CROSS OVER TO POSSESS", "A LAND OF HILLS AND VALLEYS", "A LAND WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD SEEKS" (11:11-12), "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU INTO A GOOD LAND", "A LAND OF BROOKS OF WATER", "A LAND OF WHEAT AND BARLEY", "A LAND OF OLIVE OIL AND HONEY", "A LAND WHERE YOU SHALL NOT EAT BREAD IN POVERTY", "A LAND WHOSE STONES ARE IRON" (8:7-9), "FOR THE GOOD LAND WHICH HE HAS GIVEN YOU" (8:10), "A LAND FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY" (11:9) — TWELVE. THE TEACHING SAYS "A LAND OF HILLS AND VALLEYS": HILLS — MANY HILLS; VALLEYS — MANY VALLEYS. The row on 11:11 ({SP_(39, 4, "שתים", "עשרה", "ארצות", "נתנו")} "twelve lands were given"): THE CHAPTER\'S "LAND" COUNTED — seven of the twelve are chapter 8\'s own clauses (8:7 two, 8:8 two, 8:9 two, 8:10 one); the ink: "land" six tokens in 8:7-9 and "the land" one at 8:10 (computed — the seven clauses the shelf enumerates), the seven species\' verse 8:8 giving two of the twelve ("a land of wheat and barley", "a land of olive oil and honey"). The middah: E10 — the repeated "land" read as a count, each repetition a land. THE RANGE CITATION "(דברים ח ז-י)" asserted by string; the English cites the seven clauses one by one (seven "(Dt.8:" — asserted). Fresh in both files.')
orow(39, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'SINCE THE HILL\'S SOIL IS THIN AND THE VALLEY\'S RICH, MIGHT THE WATER WASH THE SOIL TO THE VALLEY AND THE VALLEY LACK WATER? THE TEACHING SAYS "A LAND OF HILLS AND VALLEYS" — THE HILL AS IT IS, THE VALLEY AS IT IS; AND SO IT SAYS "ASK OF THE LORD RAIN IN THE TIME OF THE LATTER RAIN" (ZECHARIAH 10:1). The row on 11:11 ({SP_(39, 6, "הר", "לפי", "מה", "שהוא", "ובקעה", "לפי", "מה")} "the hill as it is and the valley as it is"): THE DIVISION DIFFERENCE — the Hebrew\'s 39:6 is this one question (Zechariah its proof, no citation of chapter 8), while the English\'s 39:6 runs on through the Hebrew\'s 39:7 and 39:8 (the rain, the irrigation with 8:7\'s "brooks of water", the snow, the dew); the citation of 8:7 the English carries here the Hebrew carries at 39:8 (asserted in both files) — each file\'s own row read whole, neither counted twice. Fresh in both files.')
orow(39, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'OR, SINCE IT DRINKS RAIN WATER, DOES IT NOT DRINK IRRIGATION WATER? THE TEACHING SAYS "FROM THE RAIN OF HEAVEN IT DRINKS WATER" (11:11) — WHEN IT SAYS "WATER", IT DRINKS IRRIGATION WATER TOO; AND SO IT SAYS "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU INTO A GOOD LAND, A LAND OF BROOKS OF WATER" (8:7). The row on 11:11 ({SP_(39, 8, "כשהוא", "אומר", "מים", "אף", "מי", "שלוחים", "שותה")} "when it says water, it drinks irrigation water too"): 8:7\'s "brooks of water" the proof that the Land drinks from below as from above — the extra "water" of 11:11 read as an inclusion and 8:7 its warrant; the ink: "brooks of water" 8:7, 10:7 (Jotbah), Jeremiah 31:9 (computed); Onkelos makes 8:7\'s brooks "FLOWING brooks" (one seat). The middah: E10 — the word "water" beside "the rain of heaven" read as an inclusion. Fresh in both files.')
orow(40, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "FROM THE BEGINNING OF THE YEAR TO THE END OF THE YEAR" (11:12) — IS THERE FRUIT IN THE FIELD FROM THE YEAR\'S START TO ITS END? RATHER, THEY ARE IN MY POWER TO BLESS IN THE HOUSE AS I BLESS IN THE FIELD (28:8; HAGGAI 2:19); WHENCE EVEN IN THE STORE? (28:3); EVEN IN THE DOUGH? (28:5); EVEN IN GOING IN AND OUT? (28:6); EVEN IN EATING AND SATISFACTION? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED AND BLESS" (8:10); EVEN WHEN IT GOES DOWN INTO YOUR BOWELS? "AND I WILL REMOVE SICKNESS FROM YOUR MIDST" (EXODUS 23:25) — NO WORM AND NO ROT IN THE FRUIT, NO WINE SOURING, NO OIL STINKING. The row on 11:12 ({SP_(40, 10, "מנין", "אף", "באכילה", "ובשביעה")} "whence even in eating and satisfaction?"): 8:10\'s "eat and be satisfied" READ AS A BLESSING\'S SEAT — the satisfaction inside the eater, the last of a ladder of six places the blessing reaches (the field, the store, the dough, the door, the meal, the bowels), the chapter\'s verse the fifth rung and Exodus 23:25 the sixth (the angel\'s clauses — chapter 7\'s kin); the ink: "and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless" ONE seat, "eat and be satisfied" six in the book (computed). The compile\'s row: the blessing after the meal (Berakhot 48b) — 8:10 the Torah\'s one command to bless the LORD. Fresh in both files.')
orow(43, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED; TAKE HEED TO YOURSELVES LEST YOUR HEART BE DECEIVED" (11:15-16) — HE SAID TO THEM: BEWARE LEST YOU REBEL AGAINST THE ALL-PRESENT, FOR A MAN REBELS AGAINST THE ALL-PRESENT ONLY OUT OF SATIETY, AS IT SAYS "LEST YOU EAT AND BE SATISFIED AND BUILD GOOD HOUSES AND DWELL, AND YOUR HERDS AND FLOCKS MULTIPLY, AND SILVER AND GOLD MULTIPLY FOR YOU" (8:12-13) — WHAT DOES IT SAY? "AND YOUR HEART BE LIFTED UP AND YOU FORGET THE LORD YOUR GOD" (8:14). LIKEWISE "WHEN I BRING HIM INTO THE LAND … FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY" (31:20) — "AND HE WILL TURN TO OTHER GODS"; LIKEWISE "THE PEOPLE SAT TO EAT AND DRINK" (EXODUS 32:6) — "THEY MADE A MOLTEN CALF" (32:8). The row on 11:15-16 ({SP_(43, 7, "שאין", "אדם", "מורד", "במקום", "אלא", "מתוך", "שובע")} "for a man rebels against the All-Present only out of satiety"): 8:12-14 READ AS THE RULE\'S PROOF — satiety, then the lifted heart, then the forgetting: the chapter\'s "lest" clause the sequence the shelf makes a law of human nature, with 31:20 and the calf as its two other exhibits; the ink: "lest you eat and be satisfied" ONE, "and your heart be lifted up" ONE (17:20 the king\'s heart, Hosea 13:6 the same sequence — computed); 8:12 through 8:14 one sentence in the ink (the "lest" of 8:12 governing to 8:14 — the consecutive perfects of 8:14). THE RANGE CITATION "(דברים ח יב-יג)" asserted by string; the English cites 8:13-14 and 8:14. The compile\'s row: the heart lifted up (Sotah 4b-5a). Fresh in both files.')
orow(48, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "FOR IF YOU SURELY KEEP ALL THIS COMMANDMENT" (11:22) — WHENCE THAT ONE WHO HEARS A WORD OF TORAH FIRST BY FIRST AND KEEPS IT, AS THE FIRST ARE KEPT IN HIS HAND SO THE LAST ARE KEPT? "IF YOU SURELY KEEP". AND WHENCE THAT ONE WHO HEARS FIRST BY FIRST AND FORGETS IT, AS THE FIRST ARE NOT KEPT SO THE LAST ARE NOT KEPT? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND IT SHALL BE, IF YOU SURELY FORGET" (8:19); YOU DO NOT LIFT YOUR EYES FROM IT BEFORE IT IS GONE — "WILL YOU SET YOUR EYES ON IT AND IT IS NOT" (PROVERBS 23:5); AND IT IS WRITTEN IN THE SCROLL OF THE PIOUS: A DAY YOU LEAVE ME, TWO DAYS I LEAVE YOU. The row on 11:22 ({SP_(48, 8, "ומנין", "שאם", "שומע", "ראשון", "ראשון", "ומשכחו")} "and whence that if he hears first by first and forgets it"): 8:19\'s DOUBLED VERB READ AS A TEACHING — "if you SURELY forget" (the infinitive absolute with its verb) made the forgetting that compounds, the mirror of 11:22\'s "if you SURELY keep" (the same form): the two doublings paired, one for the keeping that keeps, one for the forgetting that loses; the ink: "if you surely forget" ONE seat, the infinitive absolute of the forget-verb the lemma\'s ONE such form in the Bible (computed on the morphology); the scroll named "of the pious" in the Hebrew (the English\'s note reads a different name). The middah: E10 — the doubled verb read as a teaching. Fresh in both files.')
orow(48, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "FOR IF YOU SURELY KEEP" — LEST YOU SAY, I WILL LEARN A HARD SECTION AND LEAVE THE EASY: THE TEACHING SAYS "FOR IT IS NOT AN EMPTY THING FOR YOU" (32:47) — THE THING YOU CALL EMPTY IS YOUR LIFE. LEST YOU SAY, I HAVE LEARNED LAWS, ENOUGH: THE TEACHING SAYS "THE COMMANDMENT", "THE COMMANDMENT", "ALL THE COMMANDMENT" — LEARN MIDRASH, LAWS AND HOMILIES; AND SO IT SAYS "FOR NOT BY BREAD ALONE DOES MAN LIVE" (8:3) — THIS IS MIDRASH; "BUT BY EVERYTHING THAT PROCEEDS FROM THE MOUTH OF THE LORD" — THESE ARE THE LAWS AND THE HOMILIES; AND SO IT SAYS "BE WISE, MY SON" (PROVERBS 27:11), "MY SON, IF YOUR HEART IS WISE, MY HEART TOO WILL REJOICE" (23:15) — R. SHIMON SON OF MENASYA: "TOO" INCLUDES HIS FATHER IN HEAVEN. The row on 11:22 ({SP_(48, 10, "זה", "מדרש")} "this is midrash"; {SP_(48, 10, "אלו", "הלכות", "והגדות")} "these are the laws and the homilies"): 8:3 READ AS THE CURRICULUM — "bread" the midrash (the verse\'s exposition), "everything that proceeds from the mouth of the LORD" the laws and the homilies: the verse\'s two halves two kinds of study, the chapter\'s "man" the student; the ink: "not by bread alone" ONE, "everything that proceeds from the mouth of the LORD" ONE, "the mouth of the LORD" twenty-five Torah seats (the journeys\' formula — 8:3 the one where the mouth\'s issue is the food) (computed); 8:1\'s "all the commandment" the row\'s own text (eight seats, all this book\'s). Onkelos at 8:3: "everything that proceeds from THE WORD (Memra) of the LORD" — the mouth made the Memra. Fresh in both files.')
orow(53, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEE, I SET BEFORE YOU TODAY A BLESSING AND A CURSE" (11:26) — WHY SAID? BECAUSE "LIFE AND DEATH I HAVE SET BEFORE YOU" (30:19): LEST ISRAEL SAY, SINCE THE ALL-PRESENT SET TWO WAYS BEFORE US LET US WALK IN WHICHEVER WE PLEASE — "AND YOU SHALL CHOOSE LIFE". A PARABLE: A MAN AT A CROSSROADS BEFORE TWO PATHS, ONE SMOOTH AT ITS START AND THORNS AT ITS END, ONE THORNS AT ITS START AND SMOOTH AT ITS END, WARNING THE PASSERS-BY. SO MOSES SAID TO ISRAEL: YOU SEE THE WICKED PROSPER IN THIS WORLD? TWO OR THREE DAYS THEY PROSPER AND THEIR END IS TO REGRET (PROVERBS 24:20; ECCLESIASTES 4:1, 5; PROVERBS 4:19). YOU SEE THE RIGHTEOUS SUFFER IN THIS WORLD? TWO OR THREE DAYS THEY SUFFER AND THEIR END IS TO REJOICE, AS IT SAYS "TO DO YOU GOOD IN YOUR END" (8:16), "BETTER THE END OF A THING THAN ITS BEGINNING" (ECCLESIASTES 7:8), "TO GIVE YOU AN END AND A HOPE" (JEREMIAH 29:11), "THE PATH OF THE RIGHTEOUS IS AS THE LIGHT OF DAWN" (PROVERBS 4:18). The row on 11:26 ({SP_(53, 1, "וסופם", "לשמח", "באחרונה")} "and their end is to rejoice at the last"): 8:16\'s "TO DO YOU GOOD IN YOUR END" READ AS THE RIGHTEOUS MAN\'S PATH — the manna\'s hunger the thorns at the start, the good at the end the smooth road; the chapter\'s two purposes (8:2 "to humble you, to test you"; 8:16 "to do you good in your end") the parable\'s two stages; the ink: "to do you good in your end" ONE seat, "end" the lemma\'s ten Torah seats (Jacob\'s, Balaam\'s, 4:30, 8:16, 11:12, 31:29, 32:20, 32:29) (computed); the English\'s citation form "(be\'akharitecha; Dt.8:16)" — the regex misses it, the Hebrew\'s "(דברים ח טז)" ("Deuteronomy 8:16") found the row. Onkelos: "to do good to you in your END" (one seat). Fresh in both files.')
orow(297, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL TAKE OF THE FIRST OF ALL THE FRUIT OF THE GROUND" (26:2) — MIGHT ALL FRUITS BE LIABLE TO FIRST-FRUITS? "OF THE FIRST" AND NOT ALL THE FIRST. WHICH KIND IS LIABLE AND WHICH EXEMPT? I REASON: IT SAYS "BRING" FIRST-FRUITS OF THE COMMUNITY AND "BRING" FIRST-FRUITS OF THE INDIVIDUAL — AS THE COMMUNITY\'S (LEVITICUS 23:17) ARE OF THE SEVEN KINDS, SO THE INDIVIDUAL\'S ARE OF THE SEVEN KINDS; AS THERE WHEAT AND BARLEY, SO HERE WHEAT AND BARLEY — WHENCE THE OTHER KINDS? "THE FIRST-FRUITS OF YOUR GROUND" (EXODUS 23:19) INCLUDED; AFTER SCRIPTURE INCLUDED IT EXCLUDED — JUDGE ONLY BY THE FIRST ARGUMENT: AS THE COMMUNITY\'S ARE OF THE SEVEN KINDS BY WHICH THE LAND IS PRAISED, SO THE INDIVIDUAL\'S ARE OF THE SEVEN KINDS BY WHICH THE LAND IS PRAISED — AND THESE ARE THEY: "WHEAT AND BARLEY AND VINE AND FIG AND POMEGRANATE, A LAND OF OLIVE OIL AND HONEY" (8:8). The row on 26:2 ({SP_(297, 4, "משבעת", "המינים", "האמורים", "בשבח", "הארץ")} "of the seven kinds said in the praise of the Land"): 8:8 READ AS THE LIST THAT FIXES A LAW — the first-fruits\' kinds are the seven of the Land\'s praise, and the praise is this verse; the ink: 8:8 ALONE in the Bible holds all seven lemmas (three or more at five other seats; the Land\'s praise the shelf\'s phrase for the verse) (computed on the lemmas); "honey" the date\'s in the shelf\'s reading (Mishnah Bikkurim 1:3 — the compile\'s row), the ink\'s honey without milk. The middah: I2 (gezerah shavah — "bring" and "bring", the community\'s first-fruits and the individual\'s, the shared verb licensing the transfer of the seven kinds; the "the first / not all the first" a limitation). The compile\'s rows: Bikkurim 1:3, 1:10; Berakhot 41a-b (the order of blessings by this verse\'s order — the two "land"s). Fresh in both files.')
orow(313, 15, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND IN THE WASTE, A HOWLING WILDERNESS" (32:10) — THESE ARE THE FOUR KINGDOMS, AS IT SAYS "WHO LED YOU THROUGH THE GREAT AND TERRIBLE WILDERNESS" (8:15). The row on 32:10 ({SP_(313, 15, "אלו", "ארבע", "מלכיות")} "these are the four kingdoms"): 8:15\'s wilderness read as the exiles — the chapter\'s "great and terrible" (1:19\'s phrase for the same wilderness — computed) made the four empires\' waste; Onkelos reads 32:10\'s waste with 8:15\'s own words ("a house of thirst", "a place where there is no water" — the two seats, computed). Fresh in both files.')
orow(318, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND JESHURUN GREW FAT AND KICKED" (32:15) — OUT OF SATIETY THEY REBEL. SO THE GENERATION OF THE FLOOD REBELLED ONLY OUT OF FOOD AND DRINK AND EASE (JOB 21:9 …); SO THE MEN OF THE TOWER, OUT OF EASE (GENESIS 11:1); SO THE MEN OF SODOM, OUT OF FOOD (JOB 28:5; EZEKIEL 16:48); RABBAN GAMLIEL, R. JOSHUA, R. ELAZAR SON OF AZARIAH AND R. AKIVA ENTERING ROME …; SO THE MEN OF THE WILDERNESS, OUT OF FOOD AND DRINK ("THE PEOPLE SAT TO EAT AND DRINK", EXODUS 32:6 — "THEY TURNED ASIDE QUICKLY", 32:8). THE HOLY ONE SAID TO MOSES: TELL ISRAEL, WHEN YOU ENTER THE LAND YOU WILL REBEL ONLY OUT OF EATING AND DRINKING AND EASE (31:20); MOSES SAID TO ISRAEL: WHEN YOU ENTER THE LAND YOU WILL REBEL ONLY OUT OF EATING AND DRINKING AND EASE, AS IT SAYS "LEST YOU EAT AND BE SATISFIED" (8:12), "AND YOUR HERDS AND YOUR FLOCKS MULTIPLY" (8:13), "AND YOUR HEART BE LIFTED UP AND YOU FORGET THE LORD YOUR GOD" (8:14). The row on 32:15 ({SP_(318, 1, "לפי", "שבע", "מורדים")} "out of satiety they rebel"): 43:7\'s RULE GIVEN ITS HISTORY — the Flood, the Tower, Sodom, the calf, and then the two speakers: God to Moses with 31:20, Moses to Israel with 8:12-14 — the chapter\'s "lest" clause Moses\' own version of God\'s warning; the ink: 8:12, 13, 14 cited verse by verse in both files (asserted), the three verses one sentence in the ink; THE COPYIST\'S ABRIDGEMENT marked in both files ("a baraita as written in Elleh ha-Devarim" in the Hebrew; the English\'s note that the lacuna is filled at 43:4-8) — the row read whole as it stands, its parallels at 43:4-8. Read before at a Genesis sitting (the Babel ledger, as a dup row of 43:4-5 on the Tower); REREAD WHOLE here. Both files cite 8:12 and 8:14 (asserted).')

